{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>Smitten his fellow in secret.</b> He is speaking of lashon hara. I saw in the foundation of Rabbi Moshe ha-Darshan: There are eleven 'arurim here, corresponding to the eleven tribes; and corresponding to Shimon he did not write 'arur — because it was not in his [i.e. Yaakov's] heart to bless him before his death when he blessed the rest of the tribes; therefore he did not wish to curse him."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:48:32.156136016Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}